  "narrative": {
    "intro": "New Jersey received $54.9M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 256 awards with an average award size of $214K and obligations fell 99.4% year over year. Historical annual obligations show much larger totals in prior years: FY22 $9.3B, FY23 $9.2B, FY24 $9.8B, FY25 $9.3B, and FY26 $9.5B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buying agency in FY2027 to date with $52.6M. CELLCO PARTNERSHIP is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $28.3M, followed by NOVARTIS PHARMACEUTICALS CORPORATION with $8.4M and DIAGNOSTICA STAGO INC with $2.5M. Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) is the largest industry by obligations in FY2027 to date with $28.3M, followed by Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing with $10.2M and Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing with $3.5M. The current fiscal year totals are partial because the period is FY2027 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations drop so sharply in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 99.4% year over year in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for $52.6M of the $54.9M total in FY2027 to date, concentrating most buying activity. Prior fiscal years each showed multi-billion dollar totals, so the FY2027 to date figure represents a much smaller slice of typical annual obligations. The current-year totals are partial because the period is FY2027 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries dominated New Jersey in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs led buying agencies with $52.6M in FY2027 to date. CELLCO PARTNERSHIP led vendors with $28.3M, and Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) led industries with $28.3M. Other notable vendors and industries include NOVARTIS PHARMACEUTICALS CORPORATION with $8.4M and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing with $10.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
